{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you, etc.</b> Why did you need to worry about an enemy and fear an enemy, until you needed to lie, and you did not remember Me?" "<b>Was it not I who kept silent?</b> In my opinion it is a verb transitive to two objects, and the meaning is: I silence in truth the one who lies — so am I and so I have been. And it is possible that the one about whom you worried — when did you fear Me? And the first is correct. And some say the meaning of מחשה is like the meaning of החשיתי (2 Kings 14) [meaning] 'I will bear,' like a person who falls silent:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:57.708760583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}